{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST parse Rust, Python, TypeScript, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML\nsources with pinned tree-sitter grammars, selected by file extension compared\ncase-insensitively. When validating outline evidence inputs, Habeas MUST report\nthe line of the first syntax error in a recovered outline. Every\nother text file MUST use a plain-text profile in which each line that is not\nblank is an anonymous outline node of kind `line`. Each supported language MUST\nhave an outline profile that maps grammar node kinds to short outline kind names\nand, for each mapped kind, states whether a node is named, and by which fields\nor children, or anonymous. Only mapped kinds MUST appear in the outline, except\nthat a Markdown profile MAY additionally recognize colon-fenced directive\ncontainers under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.fence_precedence`\nand expose them as outline nodes under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.fenced_blocks`. Such containers MUST\npreserve source ranges and containment, and MUST NOT be recognized within\nliteral code or raw HTML. Other nodes MUST be transparent, so their outline\ndescendants appear under the nearest outline ancestor. A profile MAY attach grammar siblings to an outline\nnode, such as Rust attributes and doc comments preceding an item, so the outline\ntree need not match the grammar tree exactly; attached siblings are part of that\nnode for its line range and hash. Every file's outline MUST have a root node\nfor the whole file, independent of language. Source in no other outline node,\nsuch as top-level statements no profile maps, MUST belong to the root node;\nprofiles MUST NOT invent fallback kinds for it. Comments MUST NOT be outline nodes. Profiles MUST be\ndocumented. Upgrading a grammar or profile MAY change outlines and MUST be\ntreated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged `requirements.references.outlines` adequately tested. I did this from the supplied test source alone and requested no implementation source. Each obligation maps to tests as follows.\n\n- **Seven languages, pinned grammars, case-insensitive extension selection.**\n  - `profiles_are_selected_by_extension_case_insensitively` uses upper- and mixed-case extensions (`.RS`, `.Py`, `.TSX`, `.MD`, `.TOML`). It also checks that `notes` and `notes.rs.txt` fall back to plain text.\n  - `grammar_dependencies_are_pinned_to_exact_versions` checks that every tree-sitter crate is pinned to an exact version.\n  - Per-language profile tests cover the grammars:\n    - Rust: `rust_selectors_follow_syntactic_ancestry`.\n    - Python: `python_profile_outlines_defs_classes_and_statements`.\n    - TypeScript and TSX: `typescript_profile_outlines_declarations`.\n    - CSS: `css_profile_names_rules_by_normalized_selectors`.\n    - Markdown: `markdown_profile_nests_sections_by_heading`.\n    - TOML and YAML: `toml_and_yaml_profiles_name_keys`.\n- **First syntax error line when validating outline evidence inputs.**\n  - `reports_recovered_syntax_errors_with_lines` asserts the reported line for a Rust error. It checks that a Python error is reported. It checks that the first of several TOML errors is the one reported, not a later one.\n  - `outline_inputs_survive_moves_and_unhashed_comments_but_not_edits` checks the end-to-end \"cannot parse rust source\" diagnostic with its line.\n- **Plain-text profile.** `plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes` checks that non-blank lines become anonymous `line@…` nodes and blank lines are skipped. The `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` tool test checks kind `line` with a null name.\n- **Profiles map kinds, naming rules, and only mapped kinds appear.**\n  - `profile_rules_map_only_matching_contexts_and_keep_other_nodes_transparent` shows that unmapped nodes are transparent and their descendants attach to the nearest mapped ancestor.\n  - `markdown_views_respect_profile_field_and_child_naming_rules` checks field naming, child naming, and the missing-field case.\n  - The exact outline lists in the per-language tests show that only mapped kinds appear.\n- **Markdown directive containers.**\n  - Source ranges and containment: `paragraphs_and_nested_directives_have_independent_source_ranges` and `nested_fence_lengths_and_closer_whitespace_preserve_the_right_containers`.\n  - Unclosed fences: `unfinished_directives_retain_their_body_and_leave_the_outer_closer_outside`.\n  - Not recognized in literal code, inline code, or raw HTML: `literal_code_inline_code_and_html_shield_directive_looking_text`.\n- **Attached siblings and hashes.** `identity_hashes_include_own_attached_siblings_but_not_descendants` and `hashes_skip_whitespace_and_plain_comments_but_not_doc_comments` check attachment of doc comments and attributes to the node's range and hash.\n- **Root node for every file; no fallback kinds.**\n  - `file_level_inner_doc_comments_and_unmapped_code_belong_to_the_root` and the Python test check that unmapped code belongs to the root.\n  - `no_profile_invents_fallback_kinds` runs every language and checks that no `stmt`, `block`, `node`, or `item` kinds are invented. It also checks that outlines with no mapped nodes contain only the root.\n- **Comments are not nodes.** The exact outline lists in the Python, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML tests omit the leading comments present in each source. The Markdown test also checks that the HTML comment lands in `comments`, not in the nodes.\n- **Profiles documented.** `every_profile_mapping_is_documented` checks every profile's extensions, kind mappings, grammar kinds, and naming column against `md/reference.md`. It also checks the plain-text row.\n- **Grammar or profile upgrade as a deliberate change.** Exact pins are tested. This is a process obligation with no further testable behavior.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap. The remaining untested distinctions, such as case-insensitivity for `.css` and `.yaml` extensions, fall within the same input class as the covered extensions and the same selection mechanism.",
  "references": "089c7194443af311f484992cef3e71e6acffd09d05fea074d95173058af3c3b2",
